<title>USA: Secom to buy brake machining unit.</title>
<headline>Secom to buy brake machining unit.</headline>
<dateline>NOVI, Mich. 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Secom General Corp said Thursday it is in final negotiations to buy the assets and operations of VarityKelsey-Hayes' machining facility in Milford, Mich.</p>
<p>Terms were not disclosed. The deal is subject to a definitive agreement and is expected to close October 31. The facility makes machined brake valve parts and has annual revenues of about $12 million.</p>
<p>Secom makes cold formed and forged parts for the automotive and trucking industry. VarityKelsey-Hayes is a unit of braking systems maker LucasVarity Plc.</p>
</text>
